Subject: Fail a memory import of a ColorBuffer the renderer does not know, instead of ending the stream

A guest allocation that imports a ColorBuffer asks the renderer for its allocation info. When
the renderer has no such ColorBuffer, vkAllocateMemory aborted, which (with aemu's 0002) ended
the guest's whole stream. That happens when a renderer started again after its window manager
ended and an app that was already running imports a buffer the old renderer made, and when a
ColorBuffer was closed while a guest process still named it. The guest's stream carries every
Vulkan and OpenGL ES call of that process, so one stale handle took the agent's and
SurfaceFlinger's rendering with it. The call now fails with VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE,
which the guest driver returns to the app, and the stream stays. A snapshot load keeps its
placeholder.

Applies after 0041 on gfxstream d047a57228332d995d36600792fa9ccc26cf8ae6.
---
diff --git a/host/vulkan/VkDecoderGlobalState.cpp b/host/vulkan/VkDecoderGlobalState.cpp
--- a/host/vulkan/VkDecoderGlobalState.cpp
+++ b/host/vulkan/VkDecoderGlobalState.cpp
@@ -5332,9 +5332,13 @@ VkResult on_vkAllocateMemory(android::base::BumpPool* pool, VkSnapshotApiCallInf
                     &localAllocInfo.memoryTypeIndex, &colorBufferMemoryUsesDedicatedAlloc,
                     &mappedPtr)) {
                 if (mSnapshotState != SnapshotState::Loading) {
-                    GFXSTREAM_ABORT(FatalError(ABORT_REASON_OTHER))
-                        << "Failed to get allocation info for ColorBuffer:"
-                        << importCbInfoPtr->colorBuffer;
+                    // The renderer does not know this ColorBuffer (a renderer that started again, or one
+                    // closed while the guest still names it). That is the guest's stale handle, not a
+                    // reason to end its whole stream: the call fails and the stream stays.
+                    ERR("vkAllocateMemory: the renderer has no allocation info for ColorBuffer %u; "
+                        "the call fails with VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE.",
+                        importCbInfoPtr->colorBuffer);
+                    return VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE;
                 }
                 // During snapshot load there could be invalidated references to
                 // color buffers.
